[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186203364 :answer-field/choices 17592186203365] [:db/retract 17592186203364 :answer-field/choices 17592186203366] [:db/retract 17592186203364 :answer-field/choices 17592186203367] [:db/retract 17592186203358 :answer-field/choices 17592186203360] [:db/retract 17592186203467 :answer-field/choices 17592186203472] [:db/retract 17592186203467 :answer-field/choices 17592186203468] [:db/retract 17592186203467 :answer-field/choices 17592186203469] [:db/retract 17592186203467 :answer-field/choices 17592186203470] [:db/retract 17592186203467 :answer-field/choices 17592186203471] {:db/id 17592186204102 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02680e0f-01a2-5039-ae5b-662f20597c66" "question-7bcd4936-683c-5a30-8d4e-a52d39fd01ec" "question-0446f1ce-7aff-5c2b-b94d-259fd188ab51" "question-bfb0421c-aa0c-535f-b51f-dc865b4acd28"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203856 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^4 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by ![](images/47/471a898dd8e3dca3d9e0b077a135ac794ef58293dafa33703d23490dd92d12b6.svg) with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at ![](images/55/552dda7785a5e118e9ff3afa9bf7e7201e7d3be7454e7e380c42946d60506f31.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Writing ![](images/e0/e0ec0bd3b3ed1126735e229d153c206900bdff443354b04700379343ab15e876.svg), we have\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x})= \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function $f(x) = \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n![](images/4f/4f11665969b8a11e45fe97ef4f3add0115b365642e92e21172e2245e61147f31.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1c52a19c-5a59-5b47-837b-41939417ff1a" "question-cdabeb8f-7345-59ca-9731-4ee1c58120d8" "question-ec192a53-8b67-53c4-a3ab-2010430980bc" "question-ffb6af35-3127-5869-9aa2-2d05c6e6ebee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203864 :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -7\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x} + 3\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|^2 - 2\n$$\n\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} f .$" :question/worked-solution "Using the results \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}(\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}, \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{w}) = 2\\mathbf{w},\n$$\n\n \nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(-7{w}^{T}x+3‖w{‖}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot x+3\\cdot 2w-0 \\\\  & =-7x+6w.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204104 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f23dae50-683b-52ff-a0e9-aa781506dfbd" "question-451c95de-b4df-5e7d-8a76-df474224e7d9" "question-f3cf1839-85e6-5f28-8e77-8fe8ed36b0c8" "question-cda56dfe-5f02-56af-8d87-05b17e6af869"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203874 :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -3\\left(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|_1\\right)^3  - 5\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}f.$ You may assume that $\\mathbf w$ has no zero components." :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|_1) = \\text{sign}(\\mathbf{w}), \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w}\\left(\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\\right) = \\mathbf x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(-3{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-5{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}(-3{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-{∇}_{w}(5{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-5\\cdot {∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})-5\\cdot x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-5\\cdot x \\\\  & =-9(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-02680e0f-01a2-5039-ae5b-662f20597c66" :question/id #uuid "02680e0f-01a2-5039-ae5b-662f20597c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-265756" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{4}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={b}^{T}x.\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function $f(x)={b}^{T}x$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3c062f6-4f73-5b8e-a6b1-c784680f1423"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3c062f6-4f73-5b8e-a6b1-c784680f1423" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3c062f6-4f73-5b8e-a6b1-c784680f1423" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd675729-57e9-5d57-88d8-c335295910eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b68286b5-2fee-590c-b122-56aab19b9484" "answer-4a56765c-1fb2-5ac9-b03c-6b91b632cf07" "answer-cd675729-57e9-5d57-88d8-c335295910eb" "answer-5fa819ef-a851-5a01-9e84-7de7cf518f92" "answer-6cc262f1-2338-53de-80e9-d98a45c66d7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b68286b5-2fee-590c-b122-56aab19b9484" :answer/id #uuid "b68286b5-2fee-590c-b122-56aab19b9484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a56765c-1fb2-5ac9-b03c-6b91b632cf07" :answer/id #uuid "4a56765c-1fb2-5ac9-b03c-6b91b632cf07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd675729-57e9-5d57-88d8-c335295910eb" :answer/id #uuid "cd675729-57e9-5d57-88d8-c335295910eb" :answer/type :answer.type/m